<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<xmile version="1.0" level="3" xmlns="http://www.systemdynamics.org/XMILE" xmlns:isee="http://iseesystems.com/XMILE">
    <header>
        <smile version="1.0" namespace="std, isee">
            <uses_arrays>1</uses_arrays>
            <uses_conveyor />
        </smile>
        <name>aztecsm.v6</name>
        <uuid>64a2b81d-7768-46c3-bf1a-81fc51aaa902</uuid>
        <vendor>isee systems, inc.</vendor>
        <product version="10.1.2" isee:saved_by_v1="false" lang="en">iThink</product>
    </header>
    <style>
        <model font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
        <interface font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
    </style>
    <sim_specs method="Euler" time_units="Days" isee:pause_after_rates="false" isee:instantaneous_flows="false">
        <start>0</start>
        <stop>150</stop>
        <dt>1</dt>
        <isee:analyze_mode>false</isee:analyze_mode>
    </sim_specs>
    <dimensions>
        <dim name="Dim_Name_1" size="1" />
    </dimensions>
    <model_units />
    <isee:prefs last_model="true" layer="interface" grid_width="20" grid_height="50" divide_by_zero_alert="true" show_module_prefix="true">
        <isee:window width="628" height="417" />
        <isee:security />
        <isee:print_setup width="552" height="728" />
    </isee:prefs>
    <isee:equation_prefs order_by="sector" />
    <model>
        <stock name="SUSCEPTIBLE">
            <doc>This calculates the fraction of the total population who are initially susceptible. </doc>
            <eqn>initial_population*initial_fraction_of_population_susceptible</eqn>
            <outflow>Become_Infected</outflow>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="102" y="147" color="blue" label_angle="140" />
        </stock>
        <stock name="INFECTED_BUT_NOT_CONTAGIOUS">
            <doc>This is the population within whom the disease is incubating. That is, these people are infected, but show no visible symptoms. Those symptoms typically develop in the next phase of the disease.</doc>
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <inflow>Become_Infected</inflow>
            <outflow>Incubation_Ends</outflow>
            <conveyor>
                <len>14</len>
            </conveyor>
            <display x="263" y="146" color="blue" label_angle="53" />
        </stock>
        <stock name="DEAD">
            <doc>This is the total number of people who die during the epidemic.</doc>
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <inflow>Die_From_Smallpox</inflow>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="498" y="60" color="blue" />
        </stock>
        <stock name="IMMUNE">
            <doc>This is the total population who are immune from smallpox. It includes an initial fraction of the population (if specified) who have immunity, together with those who later gain immunity after recovering from the disease.</doc>
            <eqn>initial_population*(1-initial_fraction_of_population_susceptible)</eqn>
            <inflow>Recover_From_Smallpox</inflow>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="519" y="208" color="blue" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Become_Infected">
            <doc>The spread of infection is a reflection of three &quot;biological&quot; factors, (1) the number of CANTAGIOUS people in the population , (2) the probability that a single contact will yield an iinfection,   and (3) the probability a single contact involves a contagious and a susceptible individual, together with the &quot;social&quot; factor of (4) how many contacts each contagious person has with an infected individual. The last component of this equation (Enter first infected but not contagious individual) accounts for the initial introduction of the epidemic into the city.</doc>
            <eqn>(CONTAGIOUS_AND_VISIBLY_ILL*contacts_per_day*prob_of_infect*susceptible_contacts_between_infected_and_suscept) + enter_first_infected_but_not_contagious_individual</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="182" y="150" color="blue" label_side="top" label_angle="99">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="122" y="150" />
                    <pt x="243" y="150" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <stock name="CONTAGIOUS_AND_VISIBLY_ILL">
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <inflow>Incubation_Ends</inflow>
            <outflow>Recover_From_Smallpox</outflow>
            <outflow>Die_From_Smallpox</outflow>
            <conveyor>
                <len>14</len>
            </conveyor>
            <display x="389" y="158" color="blue" label_side="right" label_angle="4" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Incubation_Ends">
            <doc>The transit time here indicates that we&apos;ve defined the length of stay in this converter as 14 days, after which individuals are &quot;dropped&quot; into the CONTAGIOUS AND VISIBLY ILL STOCK .</doc>
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="326" y="161" color="blue" label_side="top" label_angle="94">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="283" y="161" />
                    <pt x="369" y="161" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <flow name="Recover_From_Smallpox">
            <doc>This is the &quot;primary flow&quot; draining the CONTAGIOUS AND VISUALLY ILL stock.  After 14 days in this stock, some portion of the population recovers and becomes immune from ever contracting smallpox again.</doc>
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="445" y="209" color="blue" label_angle="298">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="391" y="173" />
                    <pt x="391" y="209" />
                    <pt x="499" y="209" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <flow name="Die_From_Smallpox" leak_start="0.79">
            <doc>This is the secondary or &quot;leakage flow which, after 14 days,  causes  a fraction of the CONTAGIOUS AND VISIBLY ILL stock to die after 14 days The fraction of individuals who die each day is a function of a normalized death fraction AND an additional fraction caused by an absence of care.  Notice a &quot;no-leak zone&quot; indicating that only those in the final stages of the disease (in the last 3 of a 14 day illness) were subject to mortality.</doc>
            <eqn>if CONTAGIOUS_AND_VISIBLY_ILL &gt; 0 then (added_mortality_from_inadequate_care+initial_smallpox_mortality_fraction) else 0</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <leak />
            <display x="432" y="63" color="blue" label_side="top" label_angle="103">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="386" y="143" />
                    <pt x="386" y="63" />
                    <pt x="478" y="63" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="initial_smallpox_mortality_fraction">
            <doc>You select the mortality fraction.</doc>
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <display x="496" y="98" color="blue" label_angle="233" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="FUNCTIONING_HEALTHY_POPULATION">
            <doc>This is the total number within the population who, as the epidemic is running its course, remain healthy and (for our interests) able to function fully.  Notice this population includes those who are infected but, as yet,  show no symptoms of the disease, as well as the susceptible and immune populations. </doc>
            <eqn>IMMUNE + INFECTED_BUT_NOT_CONTAGIOUS + SUSCEPTIBLE</eqn>
            <isee:summing />
            <display x="368" y="29" color="blue" label_side="left" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="initial_population">
            <doc>The initial population of Tenochtitlan is 250,000 people.</doc>
            <eqn>250000</eqn>
            <display x="70" y="340" color="blue" label_angle="225" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="initial_fraction_of_population_susceptible">
            <doc>What&apos;s the initial fraction of this population which has no natural immunities to the disease? This fraction is considered &quot;susceptible&quot; to contracting smallpox. </doc>
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <display x="125" y="359" color="blue" label_angle="231" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="prob_of_infect">
            <doc>The biology of smallpox is such that is is very contagious.  Here, one out of five people who come into contact with the live virus are likely to become infected.</doc>
            <eqn>.2</eqn>
            <display x="133" y="199" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="added_mortality_from_inadequate_care">
            <doc>This is the &quot;element&quot; in a virgin soil epidemic which probably is absent from others.  This equation says, when the sick and contagious population EXCEEDS the number who are well, that portion without any caregivers to provide essential nourishment and care will die.  Remember, those who die will be in the final stages of smallpox, having been ill for at least 11 days.</doc>
            <eqn>if CONTAGIOUS_AND_VISIBLY_ILL &gt; FUNCTIONING_HEALTHY_POPULATION then (CONTAGIOUS_AND_VISIBLY_ILL/FUNCTIONING_HEALTHY_POPULATION)-1 else 0</eqn>
            <event_poster min="0" max="1">
                <threshold value="0" repeat="once">
                    <event>
                        <text_box>Observe that the number of contagious (or ill) people EXCEEDS the healthy population.  Already weakened people unable to obtain  care or nourishment  DIE at a far greater rate than before.&#x0D;(Click on the &quot;Run&quot; button to complete the course of  the epidemic</text_box>
                    </event>
                </threshold>
            </event_poster>
            <display x="356" y="74" color="blue" label_side="left" label_angle="196" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="contacts_per_day">
            <doc>How many contacts on average, each day they were ill and contagious, did a person with disease (and/or anything with which they&apos;d had contact that retained an active smallpox virus - clothing, blankets, etc) have? </doc>
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <display x="230" y="204" color="blue" label_angle="318" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="susceptible_contacts_between_infected_and_suscept">
            <doc>The probability of an infected individual making a contact with a susceptible person (as opposed to an immune or already infected individual) is dermined by the number of susceptible as  a fraction of the total population (minus the first infected person).</doc>
            <eqn>SUSCEPTIBLE/(total_living_population-1)</eqn>
            <display x="184" y="244" color="blue" label_angle="210" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="total_living_population">
            <doc>The total living population is simply a sum of the four &quot;live&quot; subpopulations.</doc>
            <eqn>CONTAGIOUS_AND_VISIBLY_ILL+IMMUNE+INFECTED_BUT_NOT_CONTAGIOUS+SUSCEPTIBLE</eqn>
            <display x="330" y="280" color="blue" label_side="top" label_angle="31" />
        </aux>
        <aux name="enter_first_infected_but_not_contagious_individual">
            <doc>This converter &quot;introduces&quot; the first infected individual into Tenochtitlan.  The equation below indicates that individual will &quot;enter&quot; the city on the first day of the run and, more importantly, will only have become infected that day.  As such, the model assumes that 14 full days will elapse before the individual becomes contagious (Note:  contagiousness follows two or so days after symptoms appear).</doc>
            <eqn>if time = 1 then 1 else 0</eqn>
            <display x="85" y="93" color="blue" label_side="right" label_angle="344" />
        </aux>
        <display page_width="552" page_height="728" page_cols="2" isee:converter_size="large" interval="DT" scroll_y="8">
            <connector x="369" y="171" uid="0">
                <from>CONTAGIOUS_AND_VISIBLY_ILL</from>
                <to>Become_Infected</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="372" y="143" uid="1">
                <from>CONTAGIOUS_AND_VISIBLY_ILL</from>
                <to>added_mortality_from_inadequate_care</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="360" y="38" uid="2">
                <from>FUNCTIONING_HEALTHY_POPULATION</from>
                <to>added_mortality_from_inadequate_care</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="484" y="95" uid="3">
                <from>initial_smallpox_mortality_fraction</from>
                <to>Die_From_Smallpox</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="367" y="78" uid="4">
                <from>added_mortality_from_inadequate_care</from>
                <to>Die_From_Smallpox</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="137" y="188" uid="5">
                <from>prob_of_infect</from>
                <to>Become_Infected</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="219" y="199" uid="6">
                <from>contacts_per_day</from>
                <to>Become_Infected</to>
            </connector>
